ed Blasts vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, burning sensation in extremities, confusion\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, bleeding easily, blurred vision\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, anorexia\n\nPolycythemia Vera (PV) vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vis